    {
      "text": "Ariados’s feet are tipped with tiny hooked claws that enable it to scuttle on ceilings and vertical walls. This Pokémon constricts the foe with thin and strong silk webbing.",
      "version": "alpha-sapphire"
    },
    {
      "text": "There are some areas where people use the string Ariados spins for their own weaving. The resulting cloth is popular for its strength.",
      "version": "sun"
    },
    {
      "text": "It spins thread from both its rear and its mouth. Then it wraps its prey up in thread and sips their bodily fluids at its leisure.",
      "version": "moon"
    },
    {
      "text": "Every night, it wanders around in search of prey, whose movements it restrains by spewing threads before it bites into them with its fangs.",
      "version": "ultra-sun"
    },
    {
      "text": "It spews threads from its mouth to catch its prey. When night falls, it leaves its web to go hunt aggressively.",
      "version": "ultra-moon"
    }
